sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (primary) + Claude Sonnet 5.5 High (independent second assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Lauschke, Tsiairis, François & Aulehla (2013) scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) — MorphoEval overall 91.2/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py` (91.4/100, up from 60.1/100 in Pass 1; +31.3 overall). The remediated script verifies universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across 4 explant sizes R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um with invariant total phase span Phi_0 = 2*pi = 6.2832 rad (collapse max std = 9.93e-16 rad vs 2.565 rad spread for a non-scaling constant-gradient control), simulates the 2D circular monolayer mPSM LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) target-wave kymograph and geometric radius contraction R_n = R_0(1-alpha)^n (fitted scaling slope alpha = 0.1100, r = 1.0000; 4-explant empirical segment width Pearson r = 0.9997, RMSE = 0.289 um; wave velocity r = 0.9998), includes constant-velocity non-scaling and DAPT Notch-inhibition (0 segments) ablation controls, and segments the vendored vertebrate somite/PSM SEM specimen (`mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg`, mean spacing 47.14 px, CV = 0.2010), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_026_ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM.lean`. Overall 91.2/100 (faithfulness 91.0, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 88, Parameter expressivity 91, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_comparison.png: rendered output of 2014-lauschke-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1601237 B, 2775×1650 px, artifact_sha256 d9af4f6b242811a74790adc26b77d614cc1d0e6bdd1286546bd4a3dd4e8185d7 (sha256 d9af4f6b242811a74790adc26b77d614cc1d0e6bdd1286546bd4a3dd4e8185d7), spec_fingerprint 0664f71d3f534bae2179e8241d0641469c79bbe4d267f1da6ae7e8f684b90e69. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 0664f71d3f534bae2179e8241d0641469c79bbe4d267f1da6ae7e8f684b90e69; artifact_sha256: d9af4f6b242811a74790adc26b77d614cc1d0e6bdd1286546bd4a3dd4e8185d7; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM_reference.json=4b43d8d8398b7653..., datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/ex_vivo_scaling_mPSM/scout_manifest.json=ed97fcae27d8072b...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-ex-vivo-scaling-mPSM-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Lauschke, Tsiairis, Francois & Aulehla (2013) Nature 493:101-105 scale-invariant phase-gradient encoding in ex vivo E10.5 mouse tailbud LuVeLu (Lfng-Venus) monolayer presomitic mesoderm (mPSM) with invariant 2*pi phase span across shrinking radius R(t) | Linear proportional segment scaling S_n = alpha * R(t_n) (alpha = 0.11) and radial wave velocity scaling v_wave(t) ~ R(t) / T_osc across a 4-fold explant size range; reconstructed_in_script: Universal normalized phase-gradient collapse phi(r/R(t)) across R_0 in {150, 250, 350, 450} um (collapse std 9.93e-16 rad) vs non-scaling constant-gradient divergence (2.565 rad spread) | 2D circular mPSM LuVeLu target-wave kymograph and geometric radius progression R_n = R_0(1-alpha)^n with constant-velocity non-scaling and DAPT Notch-inhibition (0 segments) controls | Bilateral dorsal somite row DoG peak and inter-somitic cleft segmentation on mouse_mpsm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010); transfer_boundary: Quasi-2D radial mouse mPSM explant phase-gradient scaling compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM periodicity; does_not_claim: Subcellular Lfng/Hes7 transcriptional-translational delay ODEs or 3D fibronectin traction mechanics." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the radial mPSM Notch phase-gradient model to an explicit dynamic wavelength-adaptation feedback driven by a shrinking FGF/Wnt gradient (Lauschke et al. 2013 Fig. 4; Beaupeux & Francois 2016).",
            "remediation needed: Extend the 2D continuum disc to a discrete disordered cell-reaggregation lattice (Tsiairis & Aulehla 2016) to simulate de novo emergence of multiple mPSM target-wave pacemakers." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.912"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
}

